वांशिक वांशिक, i. e. वंश + इक, m. A flute-piper.", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["वांशिकः"], "synonyms_slp1": ["vAMSikaH"]}], "vansya": [{"id": "vaMSya", "headword": "वंश्य", "headword_slp1": "vaMSya", "fold": "vansya", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "benfey", "senses": [{"gloss": "वंश्य वंश्य, i. e. वंश + य,\n I. adj.\n 1. Belonging to a family, of the same family, Rājat. 5, 127.\n 2. Of a good family.\n II. m.\n 1. A son, Man. 1, 61.\n 2. A kinsman.\n 3. pl. Ancestors, Ragh. 1, 66.\n 4. A pupil.\n --Comp.", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["वंश्यः"], "synonyms_slp1": ["vaMSyaH"]}], "vanh": [{"id": "vaMh", "headword": "वंह्", "headword_slp1": "vaMh", "fold": "vanh", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "benfey", "senses": [{"gloss": "वंह् वंह्, see बंह् and 2. रंह्.", "gloss_language": "en"}]}], "van": [{"id": "van", "headword": "वन्", "headword_slp1": "van", "fold": "van", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "benfey", "senses": [{"gloss": "† 1. वन् वन्, i. 1, Par.\n 1. To sound.\n 2. To serve, to honour.\n --Caus. वनय,\n 1. To act.\n 2. To hurt, to kill. See 3. तन्.\n --Cf. perhaps A.S. an-winnan, to fight against.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "2. वन् वन्, ii. 8, Par. Ātm. (in the Vedas also i. 1; ii. 2, etc.).\n 1. To ask, to beg.\n 2. To accept, Chr. 288, 11 = Rigv. i. 48, 11.\n --Ptcple. of the pf. pass. वनित, Solicited, begged. f. ता,\n 1. A beloved woman, a mistress, Bhartṛ. 2, 36.\n 2. A woman in general, Vikr. d. 44.\n 3. A female bird, Kir. 6, 8.\n --Comp.\n --Cf. 1. वन्, the vedic use, and Lat. Venus, venustas, venerari; O.H.G. wunna; A.S. wyn, ge-wenian; Goth. vêns; A.S. to-wenan; probably ὀνίνημι, ὀνήσω, ὄνειαρ.", "gloss_language": "en"}]}], "vana": [{"id": "vana", "headword": "वन", "headword_slp1": "vana", "fold": "vana", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "benfey", "senses": [{"gloss": "वन वन,\n I. n., and f. नी, A forest, Vikr. d. 79 (न); Pañc. iii. d. 56 (न).\n II. n.\n 1. Water.\n 2. A cascade or fountain.\n 3. A residence, Nal. 3, 22.\n 4. A house.\n --Comp.", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["वनं"], "synonyms_slp1": ["vanaM"]}, {"id": "vAna", "headword": "वान", "headword_slp1": "vAna", "fold": "vana", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "benfey", "senses": [{"gloss": "A. i. e. वा + न,\n I. adj. Dry, Nalod. 2, 26.\n II. m., f. ना, and n. Dry fruit.\n III. n.\n 1. Moving.\n 2. A heavy sea.\n 3. A mat of straw.\n 4. Living.\n 5. A perfume.\n B. n. A hole in the wall of a house.\n C. i. e. वन + अ,\n I. adj. Relating to a wood, a house.\n II. n. A number of woods, Nalod. 3, 6.", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["वानं", "वानः"], "synonyms_slp1": ["vAnaM", "vAnaH"]}], "vanacara": [{"id": "vanacara", "headword": "वनचर", "headword_slp1": "vanacara", "fold": "vanacara", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "benfey", "senses": [{"gloss": "वनचर वन-चर, m.\n 1. A wild beast, Pañc. 255, 17.\n 2. A forester, Kirāt. 6, 29.", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["वनचरः"], "synonyms_slp1": ["vanacaraH"]}], "vanada": [{"id": "vanada", "headword": "वनद", "headword_slp1": "vanada", "fold": "vanada", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "benfey", "senses": [{"gloss": "वनद वन-द, and वनमुच् वन-मुच्, m. A cloud.", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["वनदः"], "synonyms_slp1": ["vanadaH"]}], "vanara": [{"id": "vanara", "headword": "वनर", "headword_slp1": "vanara", "fold": "vanara", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "benfey", "senses": [{"gloss": "वनर वनर (from वन), m. A monkey.", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["वनरः"], "synonyms_slp1": ["vanaraH"]}, {"id": "vAnara", "headword": "वानर", "headword_slp1": "vAnara", "fold": "vanara", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "benfey", "senses": [{"gloss": "वानर वानर, i. e. वनर + अ,\n I. m., and f. री, A monkey, Pañc. 203, 3; 206, 15.\n II. adj., f. री, Belonging to a monkey, MBh. 13, 411.", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["वानरः"], "synonyms_slp1": ["vAnaraH"]}], "vanasTa": [{"id": "vanasTa", "headword": "वनस्थ", "headword_slp